{"id": "EUVD-2026-97641", "enisaUuid": "428034c9-705c-31ce-85b0-2ed11970dbb8", "description": "SurrealDB 3.1.0 before 3.3.0 lets Surrealism modules exhaust server memory because module stdout/stderr lines are buffered unbounded in host memory, bypassing the configured module memory limit. An attacker can run an Owner-installed malicious module that writes output without newlines, crashing the server and denying service to all namespaces and databases.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:05:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:53:58", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/surrealdb/surrealdb/security/advisories/GHSA-jj89-wvrw-c4gp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/surrealdb-3.1.0-before-3.3.0-memory-exhaustion-via-surrealism-module-output-buffering"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109339", "GHSA-rj2f-8wx8-hgm5"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6b0e2284-ee12-3c17-a9ac-38a5060367dc", "product": {"name": "surrealdb", "vendor": {"name": "surrealdb"}}, "product_version": "3.1.0 <3.3.0"}, {"id": "9f271cce-97c1-3f49-842b-795767d82ae7", "product": {"name": "surrealism-runtime", "vendor": {"name": "surrealdb"}}, "product_version": "0.3.0 <0.6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "66f41c85-0514-36bc-823a-3512d631b038", "vendor": {"name": "surrealdb"}}], "isExploited": false}